- Let's get to our first guests, y'all,

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:02.910
they are two incredibly funny guys.

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:03.801
I love both of these guys.

00:00:03.801 --> 00:00:06.360
You know one from movies
like "The Hangover",

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:08.280
and the other from "Horrible Bosses",

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:09.611
as well as his recent blockbuster,

00:00:09.611 --> 00:00:11.490
which my family personally loves,

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:14.040
the "Super Mario Bros."
movie, which was incredible.

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:16.080
Together, they star in "Fool's Paradise".

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:17.100
It's in theaters now.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.066
Say hello to Ken Jeong and Charlie Day!

00:00:19.066 --> 00:00:24.066
(audience cheers)
(upbeat music)

00:00:46.146 --> 00:00:46.979
- Thank you.

00:00:46.979 --> 00:00:47.812
Was that okay? I'll just sit down,

00:00:47.812 --> 00:00:49.195
I'll sit down, I'll sit down.
- You sit there.

00:00:49.195 --> 00:00:50.280
- I'm so excited.
- We're having a polite-off,

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:51.767
right now, a polite-off.
- A polite-off?

00:00:51.767 --> 00:00:52.860
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:54.990
That's very Canadian of you, I feel like.

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:55.887
Canadians are always super polite.

00:00:55.887 --> 00:00:57.375
- I'm Korean.
- I know but,

00:00:57.375 --> 00:00:59.220
but it's a very Canadian thing.

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:00.630
I feel like they're always super polite.

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:02.640
Anyway, you just got
back from South Africa.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:03.540
I love Africa.

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:05.520
- Yes, I had the best time.

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:06.353
- Did you do a safari?

00:01:06.353 --> 00:01:09.480
- Yes, I did do a safari
with my wife and kids.

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:10.590
We went to Sabi Sands.

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:12.660
Shout out to Lion Sands Game Reserve.

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:13.590
First time ever.

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:15.110
Got to see the Big five.
- I've been to Sabi Sands!

00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:15.943
- You've been to Sabi Sands?

00:01:15.943 --> 00:01:16.776
- Yes!

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:18.870
- We'll be right back after
these messages, oh my God.

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:20.423
- It's so beautiful!

00:01:20.423 --> 00:01:22.110
- It's so great. Got to see the big,

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:23.793
did you see the big five?
- It feels fake, yes!

00:01:23.793 --> 00:01:26.314
- Yes. It feels, it does,
it's this immersive zoo.

00:01:26.314 --> 00:01:27.510
- It's like "Cue, the lion."

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:28.380
- Right, I know.

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:30.577
And the lions knew me from "The Hangover".

00:01:30.577 --> 00:01:32.443
It was amazing.

00:01:32.443 --> 00:01:33.840
Like, "Can I get a selfie?"

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:34.673
I was like, no.

00:01:34.673 --> 00:01:35.506
They're like:
(Ken roars)

00:01:35.506 --> 00:01:36.339
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:36.339 --> 00:01:37.172
I was like, okay.

00:01:37.172 --> 00:01:38.147
- [Kelly] It is a really
cool experience, yeah.

00:01:38.147 --> 00:01:39.180
- [Ken] It was incredible.

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:40.800
It was honestly the best family trip

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.000
I've ever had in my life.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.170
- [Kelly] It's my favorite
trip I've ever taken

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:44.217
with family and friends, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:44.217 --> 00:01:46.201
So wait, Charlie, you're
from Rhode Island.

00:01:46.201 --> 00:01:48.152
Which I feel like I've never said.

00:01:48.152 --> 00:01:50.043
I don't know many people
from Rhode Island.

00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:51.510
- Am I the only Rhode Islander

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:53.520
to get on this couch?

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:55.230
- But you say they keep you humble, right?

00:01:55.230 --> 00:01:56.280
Like going back home?

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:57.870
- Yeah, I'm not allowed to be famous

00:01:57.870 --> 00:01:59.661
and that's never ever gonna happen.

00:01:59.661 --> 00:02:01.717
In fact, they'll roll
their eyes and be like,

00:02:01.717 --> 00:02:03.270
"Oh, here comes Kevin Costner."

00:02:03.270 --> 00:02:05.610
'Cause that's like, that's
where showbiz stopped.

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:08.490
At Costner, you know, yeah.

00:02:08.490 --> 00:02:10.355
But it's good! It keeps
you, it keeps you humble.

00:02:10.355 --> 00:02:11.580
I love it, I love it.

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:12.630
- I love people like that.

00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:13.800
Still make you take out your trash.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.330
Yeah, I like that.

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:16.260
My family does, too.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:17.529
So, last time Charlie was here,

00:02:17.529 --> 00:02:20.010
he talked about his
first time doing comedy.

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:21.600
So do you remember your
first time doing comedy?

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.190
- Yeah, it was an open mic.

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:24.870
I brought 20 friends.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:26.940
Did well, performed the next week,

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:28.440
brought no friends and bombed.

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:30.780
So, I distinctly remember that.

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:33.544
And I stayed in medicine
for 10 more years.

00:02:33.544 --> 00:02:34.760
So, true story.
- Oh my God.

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:35.730
It like broke you?

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:37.110
- It broke me, it broke me.

00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:38.130
I did not do very well.

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:39.960
- It's so hard. I have
friends that do it too.

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:40.920
And it's so hard.

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:41.753
- [Ken] It's so hard.

00:02:41.753 --> 00:02:43.350
Just live performance and to do that.

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:44.547
And you're just there with the mic.

00:02:44.547 --> 00:02:45.485
Nothing else.

00:02:45.485 --> 00:02:48.713
Yeah, when you do well, you
feel like a million bucks

00:02:48.713 --> 00:02:51.600
and when you bomb, you're broke.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:52.433
Emotionally.

00:02:52.433 --> 00:02:53.850
- Yeah. Emotionally.
- And financially.

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:55.095
- Try doing that in Rhode Island.

00:02:55.095 --> 00:02:58.383
Okay doctor boy, make me laugh.

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:01.246
- He's good, but he's No Kevin Costner.

00:03:01.246 --> 00:03:03.810
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:05.010
- Oh my God.
- He's not Costner funny.

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:07.110
- He's not Costner funny.

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:08.100
He's doctor funny.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:09.654
Which isn't funny at all.

00:03:09.654 --> 00:03:11.040
(Kelly and Charlie laugh)

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:12.196
- So what you're, I don't know.

00:03:12.196 --> 00:03:15.300
So wait, your first really
big thing was "The Hangover"

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:17.580
and it's turning 15 next year.

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:18.632
Which is crazy.
- Wow.

00:03:18.632 --> 00:03:19.465
(audience cheers)

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:20.298
Incredible.
- 15 years.

00:03:20.298 --> 00:03:23.520
So I have to ask,
because I heard that you,

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:26.160
it was your idea to jump
out of the trunk naked.

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:26.993
- [Ken] Yeah.

00:03:26.993 --> 00:03:27.826
- Is that true?

00:03:27.826 --> 00:03:28.659
- It was.

00:03:28.659 --> 00:03:30.144
I told Todd Phillips, the director.

00:03:30.144 --> 00:03:32.370
Because I did have
slacks on in the script,

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:34.680
and I just said, wouldn't
it just be so shocking?

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:36.510
Because you had Mike
Tyson, you had the tiger,

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:37.740
that had already happened in the movie.

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:40.140
So I asked Todd, I said what do you think

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:41.700
about Mr. Chow jumping out naked?

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:43.110
He was like, "You don't
have to tell me twice."

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:47.040
And so literally he made
me sign a nudity write-up

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:50.069
that I couldn't change my mind to do it.

00:03:50.069 --> 00:03:50.902
- [Kelly] Couldn't back out.

00:03:50.902 --> 00:03:52.062
- Yeah, I couldn't back out.

00:03:52.062 --> 00:03:53.728
- You said it! You said you would do it!

00:03:53.728 --> 00:03:54.561
- You said it, you said it.

00:03:54.561 --> 00:03:55.717
- I got it here, in contract.

00:03:55.717 --> 00:03:57.210
- Costner would do it!

00:03:57.210 --> 00:03:58.890
Yeah. I go, okay.

00:03:58.890 --> 00:03:59.956
- Are you brave enough?

00:03:59.956 --> 00:04:01.800
It was so, it was amazing though.

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:03.630
I just love that. That's a bold move.

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:05.880
- It was really just, honestly,

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:06.925
if it wasn't for "The Hangover,

00:04:06.925 --> 00:04:09.630
I wouldn't be here between
either one of you right now.

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:11.100
I owe my career to "The Hangover".

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:13.419
- Honestly that, well you owe
your career to your talent,

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:15.420
but yes, "The Hangover"
is where we saw you.

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:16.770
But your talent is why.

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:17.603
- You're too kind.

00:04:17.603 --> 00:04:19.650
- But are you one of those people?

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:22.020
Are you okay with it? I love being naked.

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:23.760
I'm okay with being naked.

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:24.895
Like a lot of people aren't.

00:04:24.895 --> 00:04:26.640
Especially where I'm from in the South,

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:27.900
and they're very conservative.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:30.540
I am not from there internally.

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:32.552
Like yeah, I'm a total hippie.

00:04:32.552 --> 00:04:34.620
- I'm so shy.

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:35.453
- [Kelly] You are?
- Like in real life

00:04:35.453 --> 00:04:37.410
where I don't even like
taking my shirt off

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:38.243
to go to the beach.

00:04:38.243 --> 00:04:39.240
I'll wear like those tight skin,

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:41.070
like swim shirts when I go.

00:04:41.070 --> 00:04:43.380
So for me, I think just
when the camera's on,

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:45.099
I'm just locked in.

00:04:45.099 --> 00:04:46.890
- Is it 'cause you go into character mode?

00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:47.790
- I think I go into character mode.

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:49.740
So, right now I'm like,
hi, how are you doing?

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:50.573
And then action!

00:04:50.573 --> 00:04:51.930
(Ken laughs as Mr. Chow)
Stupid.

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:54.810
I don't know. It just,
it's a different thing.

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:56.937
- Okay. You just made me
feel weird in real life,

00:04:56.937 --> 00:04:58.111
but it's totally fine.
- No, I'm not saying!

00:04:58.111 --> 00:05:01.029
I'm not saying you're weird.

00:05:01.029 --> 00:05:01.862
(audience laughs)

00:05:01.862 --> 00:05:03.720
- I am, I just thought most people aren't.

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:05.130
I figured you had to be comfortable

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:06.730
if you'd do it on film, but nope.

00:05:06.730 --> 00:05:08.400
- It's not insane.

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:10.877
- I don't wanna be naked
or in the trunk of a car.

00:05:10.877 --> 00:05:12.360
(Ken laughs)
Neither.

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:14.310
- You would never do that in a movie?

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:16.737
- No, I'm shameless. I'd do it too.

00:05:16.737 --> 00:05:17.899
- [Kelly] Yeah, yeah.

00:05:17.899 --> 00:05:18.732
It's funny.

00:05:18.732 --> 00:05:19.980
- [Ken] Maybe it's
something about comedy too.

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:22.440
You know, just taking
bold choices, big swings,

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:23.273
that kind of thing.

00:05:23.273 --> 00:05:24.106
- And you know, I'm joking.

00:05:24.106 --> 00:05:26.280
I don't know that I
would've wanted to do that.

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:28.550
That was gutsy, man. Well done.

00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:29.594
- [Kelly] Made the movie.

00:05:29.594 --> 00:05:31.377
So the new movie is
called "Fool's Paradise"

00:05:31.377 --> 00:05:32.993
and you wrote it and directed it, too.

00:05:32.993 --> 00:05:34.170
You did all the above.

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:36.118
So where did the idea come from?

00:05:36.118 --> 00:05:38.640
- I started writing it almost 10 years ago

00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:39.810
between seasons of "Sunny".

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:41.340
And I kept tinkering with it

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:44.917
and I shot it a couple
years ago with Ken here.

00:05:44.917 --> 00:05:47.192
And then I sat in the editing room

00:05:47.192 --> 00:05:50.770
and I watched Ken's
performance and I said:

00:05:50.770 --> 00:05:53.171
Ken, you are the greatest thing

00:05:53.171 --> 00:05:56.820
that I've ever pointed a camera towards.

00:05:56.820 --> 00:05:58.029
Can I get you back,

00:05:58.029 --> 00:06:00.960
and can I make this
entire movie about you?

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:04.413
And you said yes.

00:06:04.413 --> 00:06:07.680
And I went back in and I retooled it

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:11.370
to be this sort of funny,
sort of almost bromance

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:12.600
between these two guys.

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:16.950
But it's loosely based on
Peter Sellers' "Being There"

00:06:16.950 --> 00:06:19.050
which is my favorite film.

00:06:19.050 --> 00:06:22.110
Ken plays a down on his luck publicist

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:23.679
who just wants to be a part of Hollywood.

00:06:23.679 --> 00:06:26.460
And I play a man in a mental institution

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:28.080
who looks just like a method actor

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:29.760
who won't come out of his trailer.

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:31.800
And one thing leads to another,

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:33.960
and he sort of puts me
in front of the camera

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:37.560
and we go through a funny rise
and fall in show business.

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:40.410
But the movie is ultimately about

00:06:40.410 --> 00:06:42.180
how these two guys connect to one another.

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:44.850
And I could not have
done it without this man.

00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:45.750
- [Kelly] I love that.

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:47.657
I love that you were
inspired while doing it

00:06:47.657 --> 00:06:50.070
and it almost changed it
and made it something else.

00:06:50.070 --> 00:06:52.380
'Cause you're inspired by the
people you're working with.

00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:54.870
That's bold to change something like that.

00:06:54.870 --> 00:06:55.770
That's really cool.

00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:57.990
- The movie was speaking
to me and telling me

00:06:57.990 --> 00:07:02.340
it wanted to be as much Ken's
movie as it was my story.

00:07:02.340 --> 00:07:04.410
And I said, okay, we have to change this.

00:07:04.410 --> 00:07:07.211
And this man delivers a
performance in this film.

00:07:07.211 --> 00:07:10.139
Like nothing, with his clothes on.

00:07:10.139 --> 00:07:13.170
(Kelly laughs)

00:07:13.170 --> 00:07:14.447
- But second to his nudity,

00:07:14.447 --> 00:07:16.230
(Ken laughs)

00:07:16.230 --> 00:07:20.580
he delivers emotional nudity and hilarity.

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:21.960
- Emotional nudity, nice.

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:23.013
- I think Ken gives a performance

00:07:23.013 --> 00:07:26.190
unlike we've seen him
give before in this film.

00:07:26.190 --> 00:07:29.400
And I really hope that,
you know, people see it

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:31.140
and that he gets the
recognition he deserves

00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:32.100
for his hard work.

00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:33.062
- That's so great.

00:07:33.062 --> 00:07:34.129
(audience applauds)

00:07:34.129 --> 00:07:34.962
I love that.

00:07:34.962 --> 00:07:36.971
Well, this cast is insane.

00:07:36.971 --> 00:07:39.169
Literally. Let's just name some of them

00:07:39.169 --> 00:07:40.830
and you tell me what comes to mind.

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:42.540
So, I'm gonna start with John Malkovich.

00:07:42.540 --> 00:07:45.112
Were you nervous directing John Malkovich?

00:07:45.112 --> 00:07:47.450
- Yeah, there was a surreal moment

00:07:47.450 --> 00:07:50.440
where I needed John just to
move a little to the left

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:54.000
because he wasn't quite
standing where the light hits.

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:57.420
And I was like, how do I
tell America's greatest actor

00:07:57.420 --> 00:07:59.910
I want him to do something differently?

00:07:59.910 --> 00:08:01.785
But in terms of his
ability to say the lines,

00:08:01.785 --> 00:08:03.501
no, I left him alone.

00:08:03.501 --> 00:08:05.100
(Ken laughs)

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:06.600
- I would imagine that
would've been tough.

00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:07.800
So maybe just, oh, I don't know.

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:08.687
Maybe scoot a little to the right.

00:08:08.687 --> 00:08:10.620
You're like nervous about saying it.

00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:13.080
- Great, one more time,
John. And on your mark.

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:13.913
Just so the camera can see you.

00:08:13.913 --> 00:08:15.472
- [Kelly] Just on your mark.

00:08:15.472 --> 00:08:16.337
(Kelly and Charlie laugh)

00:08:16.337 --> 00:08:21.337
- So you want me on my mark.
On my left or my right?

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:23.400
- That's pretty good.

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:24.318
- And scene.

00:08:24.318 --> 00:08:25.817
- And scene.

00:08:25.817 --> 00:08:28.380
- I worked on that for nine months, guys.

00:08:28.380 --> 00:08:30.120
I need some flowers.

00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:31.588
- Gimme my flowers now.
- Gimme my flowers.

00:08:31.588 --> 00:08:33.720
(Kelly laughs)

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:35.340
- So Kate Beckinsale?

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:36.990
- [Charlie] Kate. Right, now.

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:39.840
I knew Kate was funny
because if you follow her

00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:41.760
on social media, she's hilarious.

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:42.593
- Hysterical.

00:08:42.593 --> 00:08:44.700
- But she, I hadn't seen her in comedies

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:46.680
or if she's been in
them, I've missed them.

00:08:46.680 --> 00:08:50.400
So I was like, I would like the chance.

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:53.640
I had a lunch with her and
I said, I have this role

00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:54.820
and it's a big role in the movie.

00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:56.550
And it's very, very funny

00:08:56.550 --> 00:08:58.650
but you have to do it very seriously.

00:08:58.650 --> 00:09:01.290
And would you be willing to do this?

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:02.610
And the fact that she said yes,

00:09:02.610 --> 00:09:04.890
the fact that this whole cast said yes,

00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:07.920
was one of the most sort of
flattering, touching things.

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:09.960
Because I didn't know you
and I didn't know Kate,

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:14.640
and I'd only met John once and
worked with him for one day.

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:17.100
So, it was really--

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:18.780
- That's a nervous ask, just asking people

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:20.220
to be a part of this thing you believe in.

00:09:20.220 --> 00:09:21.581
- Yeah, but I did believe in it.

00:09:21.581 --> 00:09:24.300
And I believed in them.
They have a lot of talent.

00:09:24.300 --> 00:09:25.800
- [Kelly] Yeah, we've heard of them.

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:26.670
They're gonna love it.

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:28.230
What was, I'm just
curious, speaking of music,

00:09:28.230 --> 00:09:29.340
what was your first concert?

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:30.840
'Cause we've talked a
lot with music with you.

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:31.740
- [Charlie] Okay. Yeah.

00:09:31.740 --> 00:09:34.650
So my first concert, and I
was trying to think of this.

00:09:34.650 --> 00:09:36.780
I think it was Natalie Merchant.

00:09:36.780 --> 00:09:37.860
- Whoa!

00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:38.793
- And I think my friends and I--

00:09:38.793 --> 00:09:40.800
- We have to be the same age.

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:41.633
I was gonna say, yeah.

00:09:41.633 --> 00:09:43.110
- She was playing in
Newport, Rhode Island.

00:09:43.110 --> 00:09:44.640
And I grew up in Middletown, Rhode Island.

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:48.960
My friends and I rode our bikes
and snuck into the concert

00:09:48.960 --> 00:09:51.750
'cause it was outdoors
and saw our first concert.

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:52.643
I think I was pretty young.

00:09:52.643 --> 00:09:54.630
- Yeah, wow.

00:09:54.630 --> 00:09:55.890
What was your first concert?

00:09:55.890 --> 00:09:59.380
- It was Prince, Purple Rain Tour, 1984.

00:09:59.380 --> 00:10:02.250
(audience cheers)

00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:03.610
- That's a good one.

00:10:03.610 --> 00:10:06.570
- And I was only 23 now,

00:10:06.570 --> 00:10:10.537
so I had a in utero
recollection of being in it.

00:10:10.537 --> 00:10:11.370
(Charlie laughs)

00:10:11.370 --> 00:10:12.828
- Your first concert

00:10:12.828 --> 00:10:13.661
was Purple Rain?
- My first concert

00:10:13.661 --> 00:10:14.665
was Purple Rain, yeah.

00:10:14.665 --> 00:10:15.510
- That's a good start.

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:17.432
- It's all downhill.
- It all went downhill

00:10:17.432 --> 00:10:18.420
from there.

00:10:18.420 --> 00:10:19.680
- It was incredible.

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:21.630
I still remember.
- Oh my gosh.

00:10:21.630 --> 00:10:22.800
- I still remember the White Dove.

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:24.270
He traded the Fender

00:10:24.270 --> 00:10:27.300
for the White Dove guitar for Purple Rain.

00:10:27.300 --> 00:10:30.900
It was just still in my
mind grooves right now.

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:34.104
- What a first concert.
- Yeah. It's incredible.

00:10:34.104 --> 00:10:35.763
Incredible.
- Okay. Bragger.

00:10:37.350 --> 00:10:38.183
- It was just the best.

00:10:38.183 --> 00:10:40.980
I had great seats, wonderful popcorn.

00:10:40.980 --> 00:10:42.390
- Prince looked me in the eye.

00:10:42.390 --> 00:10:46.138
- Prince looked at me and
said you're gonna be a star!

00:10:46.138 --> 00:10:47.256
I was like, thanks Prince!

00:10:47.256 --> 00:10:48.120
(imitates eating popcorn)

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:49.563
- Also a doctor.

00:10:49.563 --> 00:10:52.350
- And a doctor! Ow!

00:10:52.350 --> 00:10:53.430
- I was like, thank you.

00:10:53.430 --> 00:10:54.680
- You get all the talent.

